<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish unemployment falls to seas-adj 255,100  in July.</title>
<headline>Irish unemployment falls to seas-adj 255,100  in July.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of those claiming unemployment  benefit fell to a seasonally adjusted 255,100 in July from 255,500  in June, Central Stastistics Office (CSO) figures showed on Friday.   </p>
<p>On an unadjusted basis, the numbers claiming benefit rose to 259,041  from 254,683 last month.</p>
<p>			   Unadjusted	   Adjusted</p>
<p>Latest		    259,041		255,100</p>
<p>Previous		  254,683		255,500</p>
<p>Year-ago		  288,375		285,300</p>
<p>(No percentages of the total workforce were given.)</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom + 353 1 676 9775</p>
